Variable Settings
"drink" is a structure with attributes "type", "size" such that:
    "type" is a string with range {Espresso, Americano}
    "size" is a string with range {Small, Large}
"state" is a string with range {IDLE, BREWING, DONE, OUT OF STOCK} and initial value 'IDLE'
"water level" is an integer with range [0,210] and initial value 210
"beans level" is an integer with range [0,12] and initial value 12
"max water level" is the integer 210
"max beans level" is the integer 12

Scenario 01: brewing a small Americano
Documentation: Brews a small Americano and deducts water and beans
Given the machine has a current "water level", "beans level" such that:
    "water level" is greater or equal than 105 AND
    "beans level" is greater or equal than 6
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'
When the user selects a "drink" such that:
    "drink" has attributes such that:
        "type" is equal to 'Americano' AND
        "size" is equal to 'Small'
And the user clicks Brew
Then the screen shows "state" equal to 'BREWING'
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'DONE'
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'
And the machine has a current "water level", "beans level" such that:
    "water level" is equal to stored "water level" - 105 AND
    "beans level" is equal to stored "beans level" - 6

Scenario 02: brewing a large Americano
Documentation: Brews a large Americano and deducts water and beans.
Given the machine has a current "water level", "beans level" such that:
    "water level" is greater or equal than 210 AND
    "beans level" is greater or equal than 12
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'
When the user selects a "drink" such that:
    "drink" has attributes such that:
        "type" is equal to 'Americano' AND
        "size" is equal to 'Large'
And the user clicks Brew
Then the screen shows "state" equal to 'BREWING'
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'DONE'
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'
And the machine has a current "water level", "beans level" such that:
    "water level" is equal to stored "water level" - 210 AND
    "beans level" is equal to stored "beans level" - 12

Scenario 03: ordering is rejected when there are no beans
Given the machine has a current "beans level" equal to 0
When the user selects a "drink"  # any drink would do!
And the user clicks Brew
Then the screen shows an error banner indicating no beans
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'OUT OF STOCK'  # after this, I can't brew coffee anymore!

Scenario 04: ordering is rejected when there is no water
Given the machine has a current "water level" equal to 0
When the user selects a "drink"  # any drink would do!
And the user clicks Brew
Then the screen shows an error banner indicating no water
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'OUT OF STOCK'   # after this, I can't brew coffee anymore!

Scenario 05: the user refills coffee beans
Documentation: Refills the beans level to its maximum.
When the user clicks on beans refill
Then the machine has a current "beans level" equal to "max beans level"
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'

Scenario 06: the user refills water level
Documentation: Refills the water level to its maximum.
When the user refills the water tank
Then the machine has a current "water level" equal to "max water level"
And the screen shows "state" equal to 'IDLE'